cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "rcrisp" in publications use:'
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
title: 'rcrisp: Automate the Delineation of Urban River Spaces'
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.32614/CRAN.package.rcrisp
identifiers:
- type: url
  value: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15793526
abstract: Provides tools to automate the morphological delineation of riverside urban
  areas based on a method introduced in Forgaci (2018) <https://doi.org/10.7480/abe.2018.31>.
  Delineation entails the identification of corridor boundaries, segmentation of the
  corridor, and delineation of the river space using two-dimensional spatial information
  from street network data and digital elevation data in a projected CRS. The resulting
  delineation can be used to characterise spatial phenomena that can be related to
  the river as a central element.
